{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01TcKHEx6jT9XXdGrmVSGgUe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to understand what needs to be done.\n\n## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nThe project is `go-unix-utils`, a specification-driven pipeline that:\n1. Derives formal specs from C source code of Unix utilities\n2. Generates Go implementations from those specs using AI\n3. Verifies parity via differential testing against reference binaries\n\n## Step 2: Summarize Project State\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge in observable behavior.\n\n**Architecture**:\n- `cmd/` - Go implementation of each utility\n- `pkg/sys/` - Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions\n\n\n- `pkg/format/` - Shared output formatting\n- `pkg/testutils/` - Differential testing harness\n- `magefiles/` - Mage build targets (orchestrator boundary)\n- `docs/` - Specs, PRDs, use cases, test suites\n\n**Current State**:\n- Code exists at generation-merged tags for: pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/wc, cmd/cat, cmd/sponge\n- Working branch has specs only, no generated code\n- All use cases show `codestatus: not started`\n\n**Releases**: rel\n\n00.0 covers foundational infrastructure (magefiles, format, sys, testutils), followed by rel01.1 for cat, rel01.2 for sponge, rel01.3 for du, and rel02.0 for trivial utilities.\n\nSince I'm constrained to release 00.0, I need to focus on the four use cases there: magefiles (spec complete, code not started) and format (spec implemented, code not started), along with sys and testutils.\n\nLooking at the dependency ordering, I should prioritize libraries before consumers and types before implementations. The design decision about the generation pipeline means magefiles only targets cmd/version since the rest comes from cobbler-scaffold, so that's a more focused scope than it initially appe