{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01TcKHEx6jT9XXdGrmVSGgUe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nThe project_context provides inline documentation for VISION, ARCHITECTURE, roadmap, and analysis. No files need to be read.\n\n## Step 2: Summarize Project State\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities have no formal implementer-facing specs. Existing re-implementations diverge on edge cases. This project stress-tests a specification-driven AI code generation pipeline using GNU utilities as the subject.\n\n**Architecture**:\n- `docs/` — human-authored specs (PRDs, use cases, test suites); pipeline reads but does not write here\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness; runs Go binary vs. reference GNU binary, compares stdout/stderr/exit\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` — shared output formatting (tables, colors, units)\n- `cmd/<utility>/` — generated Go implementations, one package per utility\n- `magefiles/` — Mage targets; boundary between human-guided spec phase and orchestrator synthesis phase\n\n**Implementation Status**:\n- Generated code (pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/cat, cmd/wc, cmd/sponge) lives at `generation-merged` tags; working branch contains specs only.\n- `codestatus: not started` for all use cases on current branch — generation has not yet run.\n\n**Current Release**: `rel00.0` — Batch 0, foundational infrastructure. All 4 use cases have `codestatus: not started`.\n\n## Step 3: Reason About Priorities\n\n**Release 00.0 use cases** (all not started):\n1. `uc001-magefiles` → cmd/version (DD7: only code target in prd011-magefiles is cmd/version)\n2. `uc002-format` → pkg/format/\n3. `uc003-sys` → pkg/sys/\n4. `uc004-testutils` → pkg/testutils/\n\n**Dependency ordering**:\n- `pkg/format`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/testutils` are peer libraries with no inter-dependencies\n- `cmd/version` is a consumer — comes last\n- Among libraries, canonical order is alphabetical by primary file path: pkg/format < pkg/sys < pkg/testutils < cmd/version\n\n**First task**: `pkg/testutils` is the most critically described component in the architecture — the primary type `DiffTest` and its file name `difftest.go` are explicitly called out in the planning constitution (P7), giving the stitch agent unambiguous naming guidance. It is also the harness that gates all future differential test verification. I select it as the single task.\n\n**Line budget**: DiffTest struct + Run function + NormalizeFunc hook fits comfortably in 150–200 lines. Tests are excluded per P2 (split implementation and tests).\n\n## Step 4: Propose Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/testutils DiffTest differential testing harness (rel00.0-uc004)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component description, technology choices, design decisions)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml (use case flow and acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (use Glob to find prd*-testutils.yaml; read the full PRD before implementing -- it is the authoritative source for DiffTest fields and normalization behavior)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"DiffTest struct, Run helper (accepts testing.T), NormalizeFunc hook; primary exported type is DiffTest\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Define exported DiffTest struct with fields for Go binary path, reference binary path, arguments slice, stdin bytes, environment variable list, expected exit code, expected stdout bytes, and expected stderr bytes -- per all fields required by the testutils PRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement Run(t *testing.T, d DiffTest) that executes both binaries with identical stdin, arguments, and environment; pipes stdin bytes to each process; captures stdout, stderr, and exit code; and calls t.Errorf on any divergence between the Go binary output and the reference binary output\n      - id: R3\n        text: When divergence is detected, report the triggering input (arguments and stdin excerpt), the reference binary output (expected), and the Go binary output (actual) in the t.Errorf message\n      - id: R4\n        text: Add a NormalizeFunc field on DiffTest of type func([]byte) []byte that, when non-nil, is applied to stdout and stderr bytes from both binaries before comparison to accommodate known acceptable differences such as timestamps or path prefixes\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary exported type is DiffTest; source file must be named difftest.go, not testutils.go -- per project naming convention (ARCHITECTURE.yaml P7: name the file after the primary exported type)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Go module is github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils; package declaration is: package testutils; no cmd/ or other pkg/ sub-packages may be imported\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"The only permitted external Go dependency is golang.org/x/sys; pkg/testutils must not introduce any other external import beyond the Go standard library and golang.org/x/sys\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: pkg/testutils/difftest.go compiles with no errors under go build ./pkg/testutils/...\n      - id: AC2\n        text: golangci-lint reports no warnings or errors on pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n      - id: AC3\n        text: DiffTest struct is exported and contains all fields required by the testutils PRD (binary paths, arguments, stdin, environment, expected exit code, expected stdout, expected stderr)\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Run function signature is Run(t *testing.T, d DiffTest) and calls t.Errorf or t.Fatalf on any mismatch in exit code, stdout, or stderr between the two binaries\n      - id: AC5\n        text: NormalizeFunc field is present on DiffTest and, when non-nil, is applied to both stdout and stderr bytes from each binary before comparison so normalized outputs are what get compared\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15846,"cache_read_input_tokens":19189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15846},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12837782-4949-4f91-841a-1a873f204123","uuid":"9121d1e4-649a-43b0-9820-26ea2d2bb85e"}
